course: dictionary
lesson: 9008
title: Skim
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To skim means to move quickly over something without looking at every part of it. Skim has more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. «Even keen readers can be weak spellers, because reading skims words without studying every letter.» Here, skimming is reading quickly, letter by letter missed.
explain: Skim can also mean moving lightly just over the top of something. «A plate comes skimming out, straight at the Footman's head» shows the plate moving fast through the air, close to his head. Skim can also mean taking off the thin layer that floats on top, like cream from milk. Ask yourself: is someone reading, moving, or removing something?
fact: To skim a text is to read it quickly to get the main idea, without reading every word.
fact: To skim is to move quickly just over the top of something, like a bird skimming the water.
fact: To skim a liquid is to take off the thin layer floating on top.
fact: To skim a flat stone is to throw it so it bounces across water.
fact: «Skimmed milk» has had most of its fat taken out, so skim is about removing a layer.
exercise: «Even keen readers can be weak spellers, because reading skims words without studying every letter.» What does skims mean here? | Throws words across the page | Reads aloud very slowly, one word at a time | Writes every letter carefully | *Reads quickly, without looking at every letter
exercise: Ravi wants to skim the fat off the top of the soup. What does skim mean here? | *Take off the thin layer floating on top | Add more salt | Stir the soup very fast | Pour the soup into a bowl
exercise: In Britain, «skimmed milk» is red on the carton. What has been taken out of it? | Its sugar | Its colour | All of its water | *Most of its fat
test: «A plate comes skimming out, straight at the Footman's head» and grazes his nose. What does skimming suggest about the plate? | Falling straight down to the floor | Breaking into a hundred pieces at once | Moving very slowly, one piece at a time | *Moving fast, just over the top of something
test: Sam has one night before the test, so he decides to skim the chapter. What does that mean? | Throw the book across the room | *Read it quickly to get the main idea | Copy the whole chapter out by hand | Read every word twice, slowly
exam: Which sentence best uses skim to mean reading quickly for the main idea? | Maya skimmed the stone across the lake | Maya skimmed the cream off the milk | Maya skimmed her name carefully onto the page | *Maya skimmed the newspaper to find the football results
